    "originalText": "A lot of people using Figma Motion still don’t know about anchor point control and path-based object animation.\n\nAnd honestly, those 2 things alone can make your motion feel way more intentional.\n\nMost people just animate from point A to point B.\n\nBut once you understand how to:\n\n- rotate an object from a specific anchor point\n​- make an object feel like it’s moving along a path\n- fake path animation even when it’s not natively there\n\nHere's a quick breakdown on how to do both in Figma Motion.\n\nIf you’ve been using Motion but haven’t explored anchor points or path-style movement yet, you’re probably missing some of its most useful capabilities.",
